      "writtenOn": "2019-07-15T22:09:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we don\u0027t want to change this. It is an ABI change between two version of firmware. We still need this to be BIT(15)\n\nAlso ec_command.h shouldn\u0027t depend on defines in other parts of the codebase because copies of this are using the kernel and coreboot\n\nI think this flag just won\u0027t get unified and the addr_flags just won\u0027t support SPI or BIG_ENDIAN passed between firmware/kernel. Let\u0027s say they only deal in __7b not __7bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3997,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 3997,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "dfa16b6176e6ae02603fed07dca7a2d13a7a8495",
